# Marketing logic — the upsell assembler

facet app

A worked example of **business logic as a `.work` extension**: an AI-assembled, personalized upgrade
page, written entirely in a `server` block (Elixir in `.work`) and deployed onto a nexus like any
other workbook. The nexus itself ships **none** of this — it's our opinion, so it lives here, in our
own workbook, built on the platform's generic primitives (`Nexus.Llm`, `Nexus.Pricing`,
`Nexus.Capacity`, `Nexus.Live`). Copy it, change the catalog, make it yours.

## The catalog — layouts + the slots the model may fill

`data` is a typed, rendered declaration: the presentation contract. **Numbers never live here** —
the pinned tier facts (memory, bandwidth, price) come from the operator's configured tiers
(`Nexus.Pricing`), so the model can't invent them and there's one source of truth. The catalog only
names the allowed **layouts** (orderings of blocks) and the prose **slots** the model may rewrite.

data Catalog do
  layouts %{
    "focused"  => [:hero, :unlocks, :cta],
    "compare"  => [:hero, :compare, :cta],
    "reassure" => [:hero, :headroom, :unlocks, :cta]
  }

  # slot = the ONLY text the model may author, per block.
  slots %{
    hero: [:headline, :subhead],
    unlocks: [:intro],
    compare: [:intro],
    headroom: [:intro],
    cta: [:label, :sub]
  }
end

## The assembly

The org's facts come from the platform (the configured tiers + the org's live capacity reading) — never
the model's imagination. We hand the model the facts, the allowed layouts, and the editable slots, and
ask for a layout choice plus short prose. Then the guardrail strips anything numeric, and the page is
built by US from the facts — the AI's words dropped into safe slots. Two guarantees: **the AI can never
invent a number** (every numeric slot is dropped), and the page is **never blank** (the deterministic
base ships when the model is absent, slow, or off-guardrail).

`register/0` exposes this as a live source the browser calls on click; the nexus brings it up at serve
time. This `server` block IS the implementation — there is no platform module behind it.

